  "kind": "marker passive with no PassiveEffects entry; the hatch behaviour is driven by evolutionRule.type === HATCH, not by the passive",
  "summary": "Passive.HATCH itself does nothing in the pinned source: no code reads pokemon.passive === Passive.HATCH. What these 25 units do come from their evolutionRule { type: HATCH }: at the end of each stage, for every unit on the player's board whose evolutionRule is HATCH, stacks is incremented; when stacks reaches 5 (EvolutionTime.EVOLVE_HATCH) the unit is flagged to hop and, 2 seconds later (setTimeout), tryEvolve transforms it into its declared evolution (pokemon.evolution) and resets stacks to 0. A unit holding Eviolite does not hatch, and neither does one no longer on the board.",
  "triggers": [
   "Stage end: game-commands loop over player.board calls EvolutionManager.updateHatch for units whose evolutionRule is HATCH",
   "updateHatch: stacks++, then canEvolve; if true set action HOP and setTimeout(tryEvolve, 2000)"
  ],
